WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.630 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  there's never been another superhero  movie  as epic as avengers infinity war so it's  time to look into everything  that went into crafting this blockbuster  from the sheer scale of the star-studded  production to the improvised line or two  and stay tuned to find out which one of  your favorite marvel heroes survived the  snap  off-screen the road to war  according to writers christopher marcus  and stephen mcfeely  work on the infinity war script started  around january  2016. the story went through several  iterations before arriving at what we  saw  including versions written well before  thor ragnarok and black panther were  completed that means a lot of changes  had to be made to infinity war  from smaller missions to major  structural shifts  howard the dark originally made a brief  reappearance thor bantered a little more  with the guardians of the galaxy  extra backstory for the black water was  included and we even  almost saw a destructive sequence on  xander  in which thanos claims the power stone  but perhaps most intriguing of these  changes  involved steve rogers whose role in the  final cut was already pretty limited  marcus and mcfeely noted on infinity  wars commentary that  in one version of the film cap didn't  show up until the moment he saves vision  from corvus glaive  in wakanda well into the final act and  then  after we read the draft we did conclude  we're all insane  an epic production infinity wars story  spans  multiple planets and several continents  on earth features dozens of speaking  roles and a range of massive set pieces  which takes us from edinburgh to wakanda  to titan it stands to reason that the  production would be nothing short of  massive two and the numbers don't  disappoint consider that many of the  crew who worked on site had to be paid  fed and even housed and you'll get a  good idea of how big  this film really was according to  co-director joe russo in the featurette  beyond the battle wakanda  over 6 000 people worked on the film at  one point or another  all collaborating to create over 3 000  shots  of those shots 2 900 required  some form of visual effects in  post-production which meant that a  portion of the infinity war effects team  had to add something to just about every  second of the film  influences obviously the comics  themselves  had a major influence on the plot of  infinity war  but they weren't alone directors joe and  anthony russo  are of course huge fans of cinema and a  number of different films are referenced  throughout infinity war on the film's  commentary track the moment in which  ebony moore is burned while attempting  to steal the time stone is a nod to  steven spielberg's raiders of the lost  ark  a later scene in which more torches  strange with needles is a reference to  marathon man  while during interviews around the  film's release the russos also  highlighted a number of crime films as  influences on infinity war's highest  like elements including out of sight  and two days in the valley room for  improvisation  as massive as it is infinity war  required  incredible amounts of planning and  structuring in order to properly execute  the script on screen  despite that however the filmmakers  still found room for a little  improvisation along the way  for the record this was my plan it's a  nice contribution  by mr pratt in beyond the battle wakanda  the filmmakers note that the black  panther cast were performing the  wakandan war chants  off camera as a way to warm themselves  up for the action  the russos heard the chance and decided  to incorporate them into the film  not all of the new additions came from  the cast though on the commentary track  the filmmakers noted that rocket  referring to the outriders as  space dogs came from one viewer who  called the creatures that name  during a focus group discussion after an  early test screening they thought it was  funny and added it to bradley cooper's  dialogue for his rocket recording  sessions  the living and the dead infinity war  ends with one of the most  devastating gut punches in cinematic  history a montage spanning two planets  showing us the deaths of numerous marvel  favorites  including spider-man star-lord scarlet  witch black panther  and eventually even nick fury  oh no well then  it feels like a huge loss but this is  only a tiny portion of the devastation  thanos inflicted with his snap  remember we're talking about half of all  life in the universe here which means  half of anyone you've ever seen loved or  hated  in an mcu film or series naturally  the filmmakers also made sure to keep  track of which characters survived and  which disintegrated off-screen  on the survived side you've got howard  the duck spider-man's aunt may  and shuri and nakia from wakanda on the  snap  side there's the incredible hulk co-star  betty ross  the asgardian lady sif and as we later  learned  thanks to ant-man and the wasp hank pym  and hope and janet van dyne  of course it is a safe bet that none of  them will be gone for too long

